              "## Zero Tech Emitted: ZTE halts assembly lines after US govt sanctions cripple mobile maker\nToday, the threat returned, and the trade war is back on. The White House today repeated it will slap a hefty 25 per cent tariff on as much as $50bn worth of imports from Chinese factories. The president also plans to impose restrictions on investment in some companies in the Middle Kingdom",
              "The list of specific imports subject to the tariff hike will be released on June 15, with the list on investment restrictions set to be posted on June 30. While the White House has not confirmed the full list of product types that will be subjected to the 25 per cent tariffs, it did note that the tech-heavy Made in China 2025 strategy will be targeted",
              "## It's not fair\n\"For many years, China has pursued industrial policies and unfair trade practices—including dumping, discriminatory non-tariff barriers, forced technology transfer, over capacity, and industrial subsidies—that champion Chinese firms and make it impossible for many United States firms to compete on a level playing field,\" the White House said in announcing, for a second or third time, the planned tariffs"
